            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.34895/2609.34895v2/figure_3_v4.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Truncated Query Propagation (TQP).A video ofTTframes is partitioned intoMMchunks ofFFframes, and processed in order in a single iteration. For each chunk, we compute a\nloss and backpropagate it to calculate the gradients. The optimizer is updated with the average, accumulated gradients after all chunks are consumed. Queries are detached and propagated across chunk boundaries, bounding peak memory to a single chunk and preventing the model from suffering from vanishing gradients caused by long-horizon recurrence.",
